<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry VIII of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1491">1491</a>–<a href="/years/1547">1547</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Henry VIII</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry VIII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> reigned from 1509. His search for a male heir led him to break with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> and make himself head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-england">Church of England</a>, dissolve the monasteries and marry six times, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-cleves">Anne of Cleves</a>, daughter of the Duke of Jülich-Cleves-Berg, in 1540. He held Calais and waged wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england.jpg" alt="Henry VIII of England" width="320" height="562" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Hans Holbein the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:After_Hans_Holbein_the_Younger_-_Portrait_of_Henry_VIII_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
